# Client-facing chat carve-out

Extends BASE §1 *Client and analyst bodies* to evidence plans too. Evidence comments carry no TBD or a/b/c lists. A question body names the default when silence decides it, and says outright when no analyst decision is needed; a bare "Assumption (not decided)" is not an answer path (`~/.agents/kb/_shared/How-to-write-analyst-questions-with-options.md`).

Commit messages: light compression only, 1–2 sentences in the repo's style; no telegram-speak or Caveman fragments, and no license for a Caveman session default. Code and commands are never compressed.
